# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Gambaran umum {#overview}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Q-CTRL **Dynamics Simulator** is an application Qiskit Function for simulating the time evolution of supported quantum many-body models on IBM Quantum hardware. Instead of constructing quantum circuits yourself, you specify the physical model, the initial state, the time-evolution parameters, and the observables to measure.\n"
msgstr "**Dynamics Simulator** dari Q-CTRL adalah Qiskit Function aplikasi untuk mensimulasikan evolusi waktu model quantum many-body yang didukung di hardware IBM Quantum. Alih-alih menyusun circuit kuantum sendiri, kamu menentukan model fisika, keadaan awal, parameter evolusi waktu, dan observable yang akan diukur.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The function constructs and executes the required dynamic circuits and applies Fire Opal's hardware-aware optimization and error suppression workflow. The result is a time trace of expectation values for the observables you requested. Because the function applies error suppression automatically, you can run circuits at record depths and still see meaningful signals. The Dynamics Simulator delivers solution accuracy that matches the existing state-of-the-art classical tools and gives a demonstrable advantage in speed.\n"
msgstr "Fungsi ini membangun dan mengeksekusi dynamic circuit yang diperlukan serta menerapkan workflow optimasi sadar-hardware dan error suppression dari Fire Opal. Hasilnya adalah jejak waktu nilai ekspektasi untuk observable yang kamu minta. Karena fungsi ini menerapkan error suppression secara otomatis, kamu bisa menjalankan circuit pada kedalaman rekor dan tetap melihat sinyal yang bermakna. Dynamics Simulator menghasilkan akurasi solusi yang sepadan dengan tool klasik state-of-the-art yang ada dan memberikan keunggulan kecepatan yang bisa didemonstrasikan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Real-world testing achieved agreement within 1% root mean square error (RMSE) when compared against the highest-resolution classical tensor-network simulations. [Independent tests](https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.04771) from the research community have validated that the quantum computer remains accurate even beyond Q-CTRL's initial demonstrations.\n"
msgstr "Pengujian dunia nyata mencapai kesesuaian dalam 1% root mean square error (RMSE) dibandingkan dengan simulasi tensor-network klasik beresolusi tertinggi. [Pengujian independen](https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.04771) dari komunitas riset telah memvalidasi bahwa komputer kuantum tetap akurat bahkan melampaui demonstrasi awal Q-CTRL.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Two plots of classical tensor-network simulations at bond dimensions χ from 64 to 4096. The left plot shows the RMSE against time t, which stays near 0.01 until it rises sharply, later for larger bond dimensions. The right plot shows the simulation time in minutes against time t on a logarithmic scale, which increases with bond dimension.](/docs/images/guides/q-ctrl-dynamics-simulator/tensor-network-comparison.svg \"Agreement between quantum and classical simulations as the “resolution” of the classical simulation increases. As the resolution increases, both the agreement with the quantum computer and the classical-simulation runtime increase. Quantum computer runtimes are faster by up to 3000 times.\")\n"
msgstr "![Two plots of classical tensor-network simulations at bond dimensions χ from 64 to 4096. The left plot shows the RMSE against time t, which stays near 0.01 until it rises sharply, later for larger bond dimensions. The right plot shows the simulation time in minutes against time t on a logarithmic scale, which increases with bond dimension.](/docs/images/guides/q-ctrl-dynamics-simulator/tensor-network-comparison.svg \"Agreement between quantum and classical simulations as the “resolution” of the classical simulation increases. As the resolution increases, both the agreement with the quantum computer and the classical-simulation runtime increase. Quantum computer runtimes are faster by up to 3000 times.\")\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Benchmarks {#benchmarks}"
msgstr "Benchmark {#benchmarks}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The number of sites determines how many qubits are needed, while the number of Trotter steps controls the depth of the time-evolution circuits. Each lattice site uses two qubits to represent the spin-up and spin-down occupations.\n"
msgstr "Jumlah site menentukan berapa banyak qubit yang dibutuhkan, sedangkan jumlah langkah Trotter mengatur kedalaman circuit evolusi waktu. Setiap site lattice memakai dua qubit untuk merepresentasikan okupansi spin-up dan spin-down.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This workflow has been demonstrated for chains of 60 sites (120 qubits) with 30 Trotter steps, and for chains of 31 sites (62 qubits) with 90 Trotter steps. The table below shows the circuit resources and QPU execution times from the [reported experiments](https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.04025), performed on IBM&reg; Heron r3 (`ibm_boston`) device with 20,000 shots per circuit.\n"
msgstr "Workflow ini telah didemonstrasikan untuk rantai 60 site (120 qubit) dengan 30 langkah Trotter, dan untuk rantai 31 site (62 qubit) dengan 90 langkah Trotter. Tabel di bawah menunjukkan sumber daya circuit dan waktu eksekusi QPU dari [eksperimen yang dilaporkan](https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.04025), yang dilakukan pada perangkat IBM&reg; Heron r3 (`ibm_boston`) dengan 20.000 shot per circuit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| System size | Trotter steps | Two-qubit depth | Two-qubit gate count | QPU time | QPU time with REM + DR |\n"
"| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n"
"| 10 sites (20 qubits) | 30 | 152 | 1,457 | 2m 46s | 4m 25s |\n"
"| 10 sites (20 qubits) | 60 | 302 | 2,897 | 5m 36s | 8m 42s |\n"
"| 10 sites (20 qubits) | 90 | 452 | 4,337 | 8m 46s | 13m 26s |\n"
"| 31 sites (62 qubits) | 30 | 152 | 4,649 | 2m 46s | 4m 25s |\n"
"| 31 sites (62 qubits) | 60 | 302 | 9,239 | 5m 36s | 8m 42s |\n"
"| 31 sites (62 qubits) | 90 | 452 | 13,829 | 8m 46s | 13m 26s |\n"
"| 60 sites (120 qubits) | 30 | 152 | 9,057 | 2m 46s | 4m 25s |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Ukuran sistem | Langkah Trotter | Kedalaman dua-qubit | Jumlah gate dua-qubit | Waktu QPU | Waktu QPU dengan REM + DR |\n"
"| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n"
"| 10 site (20 qubit) | 30 | 152 | 1.457 | 2m 46s | 4m 25s |\n"
"| 10 site (20 qubit) | 60 | 302 | 2.897 | 5m 36s | 8m 42s |\n"
"| 10 site (20 qubit) | 90 | 452 | 4.337 | 8m 46s | 13m 26s |\n"
"| 31 site (62 qubit) | 30 | 152 | 4.649 | 2m 46s | 4m 25s |\n"
"| 31 site (62 qubit) | 60 | 302 | 9.239 | 5m 36s | 8m 42s |\n"
"| 31 site (62 qubit) | 90 | 452 | 13.829 | 8m 46s | 13m 26s |\n"
"| 60 site (120 qubit) | 30 | 152 | 9.057 | 2m 46s | 4m 25s |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For a fixed number of Trotter steps, the reported circuit depth and QPU time remain the same across the tested system sizes, while the two-qubit gate count increases. Increasing the number of steps produces deeper circuits and requires more QPU time.\n"
msgstr "Untuk jumlah langkah Trotter yang tetap, kedalaman circuit dan waktu QPU yang dilaporkan tetap sama di semua ukuran sistem yang diuji, sementara jumlah gate dua-qubit bertambah. Menambah jumlah langkah menghasilkan circuit yang lebih dalam dan membutuhkan lebih banyak waktu QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here, QPU time is the cumulative hardware execution time for the main simulation circuits. The last column also includes the QPU time for noise characterization used in readout error mitigation (REM) and decay recovery (DR).\n"
"This guide uses a small one-dimensional Fermi-Hubbard example to show the complete workflow from defining the model to plotting the measured dynamics.\n"
msgstr ""
"Di sini, waktu QPU adalah total waktu eksekusi hardware kumulatif untuk circuit simulasi utama. Kolom terakhir juga mencakup waktu QPU untuk karakterisasi noise yang dipakai dalam readout error mitigation (REM) dan decay recovery (DR).\n"
"Panduan ini memakai contoh kecil Fermi-Hubbard satu dimensi untuk menunjukkan workflow lengkap, dari mendefinisikan model hingga memplot dinamika yang terukur.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Function description {#function-description}"
msgstr "Deskripsi fungsi {#function-description}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Quantum dynamics describes how a quantum system changes over time. Studying this evolution helps you understand how particles move, how correlations develop, and how a system responds to a change in its state or Hamiltonian.\n"
msgstr "Dinamika kuantum menjelaskan bagaimana sistem kuantum berubah seiring waktu. Mempelajari evolusi ini membantumu memahami bagaimana partikel bergerak, bagaimana korelasi berkembang, dan bagaimana sistem merespons perubahan keadaan atau Hamiltonian-nya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Fermi-Hubbard model describes fermions moving between lattice sites and interacting when they occupy the same site. The competition between hopping and interactions makes it a useful model for studying strongly correlated electrons. Its time evolution can reveal how spin and charge propagate, and how an initially ordered system relaxes.\n"
msgstr "Model Fermi-Hubbard menjelaskan fermion yang berpindah antar site lattice dan berinteraksi ketika menempati site yang sama. Persaingan antara hopping dan interaksi menjadikannya model yang berguna untuk mempelajari elektron berkorelasi kuat. Evolusi waktunya dapat memperlihatkan bagaimana spin dan muatan merambat, dan bagaimana sistem yang awalnya teratur berelaksasi.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Model {#model}"
msgstr "Model {#model}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Dynamics Simulator supports a one-dimensional Fermi-Hubbard chain with open boundaries. For a chain of $L$ sites, the Hamiltonian is defined as follows:\n"
msgstr "Dynamics Simulator mendukung rantai Fermi-Hubbard satu dimensi dengan batas terbuka. Untuk rantai dengan $L$ site, Hamiltonian didefinisikan sebagai berikut:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"H =\n"
"-\\sum_{i=0}^{L-2}\\sum_{\\sigma\\in\\{\\uparrow,\\downarrow\\}}\n"
"t_{h,i}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"c^\\dagger_{i\\sigma}c_{i+1,\\sigma}\n"
"+\n"
"c^\\dagger_{i+1,\\sigma}c_{i\\sigma}\n"
"\\right)\n"
"+\\sum_{i=0}^{L-1}U_i n_{i\\uparrow}n_{i\\downarrow}\n"
"-\\sum_{i=0}^{L-1}\\sum_{\\sigma\\in\\{\\uparrow,\\downarrow\\}}\n"
"\\mu_i n_{i\\sigma}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"H =\n"
"-\\sum_{i=0}^{L-2}\\sum_{\\sigma\\in\\{\\uparrow,\\downarrow\\}}\n"
"t_{h,i}\n"
"\\left(\n"
"c^\\dagger_{i\\sigma}c_{i+1,\\sigma}\n"
"+\n"
"c^\\dagger_{i+1,\\sigma}c_{i\\sigma}\n"
"\\right)\n"
"+\\sum_{i=0}^{L-1}U_i n_{i\\uparrow}n_{i\\downarrow}\n"
"-\\sum_{i=0}^{L-1}\\sum_{\\sigma\\in\\{\\uparrow,\\downarrow\\}}\n"
"\\mu_i n_{i\\sigma}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, $c^\\dagger_{i\\sigma}$ and $c_{i\\sigma}$ create and annihilate a fermion with spin $\\sigma$ at site $i$. The number operator $n_{i\\sigma}=c^\\dagger_{i\\sigma}c_{i\\sigma}$ measures the occupation of that spin orbital.\n"
msgstr "Di sini, $c^\\dagger_{i\\sigma}$ dan $c_{i\\sigma}$ menciptakan dan memusnahkan fermion dengan spin $\\sigma$ pada site $i$. Operator jumlah $n_{i\\sigma}=c^\\dagger_{i\\sigma}c_{i\\sigma}$ mengukur okupansi orbital spin tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The model inputs specify the following coefficients:\n"
msgstr "Input model menentukan koefisien berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`hopping_amplitude`: $t_{h,i}$, which controls hopping between neighboring sites $i$ and $i+1$.\n"
msgstr "`hopping_amplitude`: $t_{h,i}$, yang mengatur hopping antara site bertetangga $i$ dan $i+1$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`on_site_interaction`: $U_i$, the interaction between spin-up and spin-down fermions occupying the same site.\n"
msgstr "`on_site_interaction`: $U_i$, interaksi antara fermion spin-up dan spin-down yang menempati site yang sama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`chemical_potential`: $\\mu_i$, the local chemical potential, which enters the Hamiltonian with a minus sign.\n"
msgstr "`chemical_potential`: $\\mu_i$, potensial kimia lokal, yang masuk ke Hamiltonian dengan tanda minus.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Supply a scalar to use the same coefficient throughout the chain, or a list to specify coefficients for individual bonds or sites.\n"
msgstr "Berikan skalar untuk memakai koefisien yang sama di seluruh rantai, atau list untuk menentukan koefisien bagi bond atau site tertentu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In units where $\\hbar=1$, the initial state evolves as follows:\n"
msgstr "Dalam satuan di mana $\\hbar=1$, keadaan awal berevolusi sebagai berikut:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi(t)\\rangle=e^{-iHt}|\\psi(0)\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi(t)\\rangle=e^{-iHt}|\\psi(0)\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The function estimates the expectation values of the observables you specify at successive simulation times.\n"
msgstr "Fungsi ini mengestimasi nilai ekspektasi dari observable yang kamu tentukan pada waktu-waktu simulasi yang berurutan.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Workflow {#workflow}"
msgstr "Workflow {#workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The function's workflow consists of the following steps:\n"
msgstr "Workflow fungsi ini terdiri dari langkah-langkah berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Algorithmic synthesis:** The function uses the Hamiltonian and simulation time settings to construct an optimized Trotter-Suzuki sequence, which reduces circuit depth while accounting for simulation accuracy.\n"
msgstr "**Sintesis algoritmik:** Fungsi ini memakai Hamiltonian dan pengaturan waktu simulasi untuk menyusun urutan Trotter-Suzuki yang dioptimalkan, yang mengurangi kedalaman circuit sambil memperhitungkan akurasi simulasi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Hardware-aware mapping:** The function maps and routes the circuits by using the qubit connectivity and error characteristics of the selected IBM Quantum backend.\n"
msgstr "**Pemetaan sadar-hardware:** Fungsi ini memetakan dan merutekan circuit dengan memakai konektivitas qubit dan karakteristik error dari backend IBM Quantum yang dipilih.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Physical-layer error suppression:** Fire Opal incorporates dynamical decoupling and pulse-level corrections to suppress noise from the environment and crosstalk during hardware execution.\n"
msgstr "**Error suppression lapisan fisik:** Fire Opal menggabungkan dynamical decoupling dan koreksi tingkat pulse untuk menekan noise dari lingkungan dan crosstalk selama eksekusi di hardware.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The function manages these stages automatically and returns the expectation values of the requested observables over time.\n"
msgstr "Fungsi ini mengelola tahap-tahap ini secara otomatis dan mengembalikan nilai ekspektasi dari observable yang diminta sepanjang waktu.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You define the physical problem and simulation settings through the function inputs. The current interface supports Trotter time evolution, where `time_step` sets the duration of each step and `step_count` sets the number of steps.\n"
msgstr "Kamu mendefinisikan masalah fisika dan pengaturan simulasi lewat input fungsi. Antarmuka saat ini mendukung evolusi waktu Trotter, di mana `time_step` mengatur durasi setiap langkah dan `step_count` mengatur jumlah langkah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For additional details, see the [Fire Opal dynamics simulator overview](https://docs.q-ctrl.com/fire-opal/execute/run-algorithms/fire-opal-dynamics-simulator) and the [`simulate_dynamics` API reference](https://docs.q-ctrl.com/references/fire-opal/fireopal/fireopal.simulate_dynamics).\n"
msgstr "Untuk detail tambahan, lihat [gambaran umum Fire Opal dynamics simulator](https://docs.q-ctrl.com/fire-opal/execute/run-algorithms/fire-opal-dynamics-simulator) dan [referensi API `simulate_dynamics`](https://docs.q-ctrl.com/references/fire-opal/fireopal/fireopal.simulate_dynamics).\n"

